do Global.stop_movement()
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(9)
set {npc_name1} = "Lover"
set {npc_name2} = "Lover"
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk: My love, where art thou?\
Like the summer breeze he forgot me!\
In vain I attempted to leave the Temple, \
for duty called and my family forced me.
Townsfolk: How stupid I've been, he left already!\
My heart swells with pain.\
Why should I keep living?\
Why shouldn't I just jump out of this balcony?
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(10)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk2: Wait for me, my love, I didn't leave!\
Until the deep of the night I waited,\
my love for you kept awake\
my body from the brink of collapse.
Townsfolk2: If you jump, my love, I too will.\
From the wall I shall jump.
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(9)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk: My love! Thou hast not forgotten me!
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(10)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk2: Forget you? Not in death\
could thy love stop pursuing me,\
my bones would stand to see thee
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(9)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk: What sayest thou? Not in a thousand lives\
even if I were to be locked behind a thousand forts,\
could they separate me from thee, my life
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(10)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk2: ¡MWhat forts or soldiers can not\
cand do some decrepit clerics,\
barely some skeletal beings,\
that forbid our love, woe!
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(9)
[wait time="1.0"]
Townsfolk: My love, please, fret not!\
Thou knowest my duty exceeds me\
without our rituals, the invisible threat\
may doom our city!
Townsfolk: One day this duty shall finish, \
and we may together start anew,\
in the meantime, I yearn the touch of your body;\
¡take this rope and come up to my mindow!
do Global.cam_switch_to_static(11)
[wait time="3.0"]
Veska: [portrait=serious](I believe something got lost in translation there...)
Veska: [portrait=serious]Its so sad they can't be together because of their social status...
set {npc_name2} = "Granny"
Townsfolk2: What? Oh! Don't worry young lady, they do that every week.
Veska: [portrait=shock]Every…?
Townsfolk2: Yeah, they used to do that every night, but neighbours complained. Now they just do it once a week.
Veska: [portrait=serious]Oh… I thought there was a world of differences between the theocratic elite and the common people.
Townsfolk2: I mean, there are… but there is no law against it or anything. It's not common, but it happens sometimes.
Veska: [portrait=serious]Hmm… And then why do they do all that?
Townsfolk2: Don't you have anyone, young lady?
Veska: [portrait=shock]AEh… Hmm… Well… I don't…
Townsfolk2: Don't worry, you're still young. Some day you'll find how beautiful it is to find someone as weird as you.
Veska: [portrait=simper]...
do Dialogic.start_timeline("check_transition_TL")
